UNRELEASED  Chris Burdess  <dog@gnu.org>

	Changes towards release 1.0.0.

	Build system: GNU Autoconf and Automake.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.am, src/Makefile.am, m4/: New.  Require C99,
	zlib and POSIX threads; pin -std=c99; WARN_CFLAGS for -Wall -Wextra
	-pedantic.  The old hand-written Makefile is removed.
	* AUTHORS, NEWS, ChangeLog, README, CONTRIBUTING: New or updated for the
	GNU layout.  README.md is now README.
	* test/: Regression tests, jtreg glue (test/fake-jdk) and the test driver
	test/run-tests.sh.  Development only; not in EXTRA_DIST, so not in the
	distribution tarball.  "make check", "make check-one TEST=...",
	"make jtreg-test".
	* src/*.c: Include <config.h> first.
	* src/genesis.h (GENESIS_VERSION): Take the version from configure.ac.
	* src/genesis.c (shared_counter_t): Replace C11 atomics with a
	mutex-protected counter.
	(print_version, print_usage): Print package name, bug address.
	(main): Accept --version and --help.

	Class file version and -target.
	* src/genesis.c (compiler_options_new): -target defaults to unset
	(automatic).
	(codegen_phase_worker): Set the target version on the top-level class
	before it is generated and written; previously only nested, local and
	anonymous classes received it.
	* src/classwriter.c (choose_class_version): New.  Compute the lowest
	version the class needs (floor 52); treat an explicit target as a
	ceiling and report an error when a feature needs more.  Omit the
	NestHost/NestMembers attributes for explicit targets below 55.
	* src/codegen.h (class_gen_t): Add is_record.
	* src/codegen.c (codegen_class): Set it.  The old ACC_RECORD test was
	dead code, so records never raised the class file version.

	Lambdas, method references and generics.
	* src/codegen.c (inner_class_access_flags): New.  Build InnerClasses
	flags including ACC_INTERFACE, ACC_ABSTRACT, ACC_ENUM, ACC_ANNOTATION
	and implicit static.  Used for the three kinds of InnerClasses entry
	here and in src/codegen_stmt.c.
	* src/semantic.c (get_functional_interface_sam): Make public.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_expr): Use it for method references
	instead of a private single-abstract-method counter.
	* src/semantic.c (preregister_nested_types): Declare a nested class's
	own type parameters before resolving its member signatures; the later
	pass reuses those symbols so the class and its members share one type
	variable.
	* src/semantic.c (symbol_from_classfile): Give a bare type-variable
	field the bound implied by its descriptor.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_method_call): Treat a field of type-
	variable type as a receiver, dispatching on its bound.
	(coerce_arg_to_param): New.  Shared argument conversion (boxing,
	unboxing, widening) extracted from codegen_method_call.
	(codegen_new_object): Convert constructor arguments with it; use the
	descriptor stored in a class file for external constructors; count
	stack slots from the declared parameter types.
	(checkcast_generic_field): New.  Cast a type-variable field read back
	to its specific type.

	String concatenation and anonymous classes.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (get_append_descriptor): Trust the resolved type
	first; append wrappers and other references as Object.
	(codegen_string_concat): Take the argument slot count from the append
	overload chosen, not from the operand's unboxed kind.
	(codegen_method_call): Compute the argument slot count once, from the
	parameter types, before emitting the call; use it for the invokeinterface
	count operand.
	* src/semantic.c (declared_inside_current_class): New.  Do not treat a
	parameter or local of a local/anonymous class's own method as captured.
	* src/codegen.c (codegen_anonymous_class): Generate superclass and
	interface bridge methods, as codegen_class does.
	* test/src/java8/{StringConcatBoxedTest,AnonymousParamTest}.java: New.

	Diagnostics.
	* src/parser.c (parser_parse): Report, and stop at, an
	unrecognised top-level declaration instead of discarding the error.
	Give a specific message for records and sealed classes below the
	source level that supports them.
	* src/genesis.c (output_class): Drop a redundant error message.

	Tests.
	* test/run-tests.sh: Precompile helper classes for every version
	directory; add class file version, -target ceiling, old -source,
	invalid input and class-file-loaded generic class checks.
	* test/classversion/, test/oldsource/, test/external/,
	test/invalid/StrayTopLevelMember.java,
	test/src/java8/{NestedGenericTest,BoundedTypeVarCallTest,
	TypeVarBoxingTest}.java: New.

2016-2020  Chris Burdess  <dog@gnu.org>

	Earlier development; see the git history.
